  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added Sage-compatible ZZ[x]/QQ[x] xgcd through two generated owned three-polynomial FLINT aggregate resources and selectors, with exact portable fallbacks, upstream Sage oracle fixtures, deterministic close/failure and sanitizer lifecycle coverage, and warm performance budgets.",
    "risks": [
      "The aggregate declarations use wasm=False because generated exact-polynomial resource ownership is not yet available in Wasm; browsers use the tested ordinary-Python fallback, matching the pre-existing exact-polynomial limitation rather than adding a new architecture blocker.",
      "The portable ZZ[x] fallback computes a Sylvester determinant with Bareiss elimination to preserve Sage's resultant-valued semantics; it is correctness-oriented rather than intended to compete with FLINT for large inputs."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate generated exact-polynomial resource ownership into the Wasm host when that shared resource path is implemented.",
      "Consider extending xgcd to finite-field polynomial parents in a separate focused lane."
    ]
  }
